# Not yet implemented — tracked as a follow-up issue once Cognito (see
# cognito.env.example) is proven out. The seam this file will eventually
# use already exists: config.yaml.template's ${OIDC_ISSUER}/${OIDC_AUDIENCE}/
# ${OIDC_JWKS_URI} placeholders and the `jwt.role` CEL check don't change no
# matter which provider is behind them, so swapping to Okta should only
# mean filling in this file and getting a `role` claim into Okta's tokens
# (via a custom authorization server claim) — not touching config.yaml.template
# or the CEL policy in docker-compose.yml.
#
# Expected shape once filled in:
# OIDC_ISSUER=https://<your-org>.okta.com/oauth2/default
# OIDC_AUDIENCE=api://agentgateway
# OIDC_JWKS_URI=https://<your-org>.okta.com/oauth2/default/v1/keys
